  "question": {
    "text": "In an irreversible process taking place at constant $\\mathrm{T}$ and $\\mathrm{P}$ and in which only pressure-volume work is being done, the change in Gibbs free energy (dG) and change in entropy (dS), satisfy the criteria",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qhEA8",
      "text": "\n$(\\mathrm{dS})_{\\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{E}}>0,(\\mathrm{dG})_{\\mathrm{T}, \\mathrm{P}} < 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "L7t18",
      "text": "\n$(\\mathrm{dS})_{\\mathrm{V}: \\mathrm{E}}=0,(\\mathrm{dG})_{\\mathrm{TPP}}=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FEa8E",
      "text": "\n$(\\mathrm{dS})_{\\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{E}}=0,(\\mathrm{dG})_{\\mathrm{T}, \\mathrm{P}}>0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "utmqv",
      "text": "\n$(\\mathrm{dS})_{\\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{E}} < 0,(\\mathrm{dG})_{\\mathrm{T}, \\mathrm{P}} < 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For spontaneous reaction, $d S>0$ an $\\Delta \\mathrm{G}$ and $\\mathrm{dG}$ should be negative i.e. $ < 0$",
